          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with onset at 62 years of age. Seizures are generalized tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately twice per week. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant and is classified as drug-responsive.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Carbamazepine  \n- Brivaracetam  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures, approximately 2 per week.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nGeneralized, drug-responsive epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures. Genetic etiology: causative SCN1A variant c.5734C>T.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue the current antiseizure medications, carbamazepine and brivaracetam, and monitor seizure frequency.",
